 "text": "In 1946, U.S. debt was bigger than the whole economy. By 1974, it was under a quarter of it. And here's the strange part. The debt itself didn't shrink. It actually grew. The economy grew around it, and prices rose too. Thing one, it borrows in its own money. A family borrows dollars it can't make. This household borrows in dollars, and the dollar is its own currency. Thing two, it never retires. A family has to pay off its debts within one lifetime. A country has no last payday. A family can't grow its way out of a loan like that. A country did. This is history, not a forecast.",
